    "done_when": "imas_ambix/data/eddb.py gains read_channel(cache_root, shot, category, dname) returning a ChannelRecord with the data, the channel's time base and its UNIT_ATTR unit read from channel_path and channel_time_path, and its module docstring names read_channel as the raw read beside the engine path instead of saying the cache needs no cache-specific reader; tests/data/test_eddb_cache.py gains a round-trip test that writes a channel with write_channel and asserts read_channel returns the same data, time base and unit; scripts/figures_jt60sa_signals.py reads only the cache under JT60SA_ROOT, takes the PF coil-current chains and the PSRC plasma current that load_packaged_signal_map('jt-60sa', 'pf_active') and load_packaged_signal_map('jt-60sa', 'magnetics') serve, applying each signal's channel_factor and taking the bound channel's unit from VirtualArray.attrs, reads every channel's time base and every unbound flux-loop channel through read_channel, and renders with imas_ink.figures.time_trace_figure_mpl in DEFAULT_STYLE, holding no colour, label or style constant of its own and drawing nothing itself; it writes exactly three SVG files and no PNG under docs/figures/jt60sa-signals/: E101154's served PF coil currents and plasma current one per panel, E101154's flux loops one panel per index holding the processed PSRC magFluxLp channel then the raw MDAC magFlxLp channel of that index with the raw one in replace(DEFAULT_STYLE, trace_linestyle=DEFAULT_STYLE.ref_lcfs_linestyle), and C060033's served PF coil currents one per panel; the script prints per figure the channel names and units it drew and says when a channel's time base or unit differs from its neighbours; docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-geometry-and-signal-figures/jtfig-signal-figures.html embeds the three SVGs with project-absolute src and captions naming the shot, the channels and their units; 'uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_eddb_cache.py' passes and 'uv run --no-sync ruf